214
00:12:23,366 --> 00:12:27,133
because this machine is way more powerful than what I have just shown you

215
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:30,866
and I just realize I never explained how overclocks work in this modpack

216
00:12:30,966 --> 00:12:33,700
and this is a machine with perfect overclock

217
00:12:33,966 --> 00:12:35,333
which is quite special

218
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:40,933
now, if a receipt, for example, this plastic circuit board which we are going to craft a lot of

219
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,500
has a processing tier of LV

220
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:49,066
that is a crafting recipe 40 seconds at LV

221
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:51,266
total 24,000 EU (per tick)

222
00:12:51,466 --> 00:12:53,266
if you use a higher tier machine

223
00:12:53,266 --> 00:12:54,600
you are going to overclock it

224
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:57,333
that means it's going to use four times the power

225
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,500
but it will take half the time

226
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,133
for a total of twice the energy

227
00:13:01,666 --> 00:13:02,466
and there it goes

228
00:13:02,466 --> 00:13:04,133
and you can do that multiple times

229
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:06,066
every time you do that

230
00:13:06,066 --> 00:13:10,566
you double the total power consumption to half the time

231
00:13:11,333 --> 00:13:13,366
and you can see it scales nicely

232
00:13:13,366 --> 00:13:17,066
but if you instead use a large chemical reactor

233
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:20,366
the large chemical reactor has perfect overclock

234
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:24,066
that means that instead of taking 20 seconds at MV

235
00:13:24,066 --> 00:13:26,700
it will take only 10 seconds at MV

236
00:13:27,466 --> 00:13:28,700
two seconds at HV

237
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:31,700
and less than half second at EV

238
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:37,000
and as you can see it's doing 10 at a time because batch mode is enabled

239
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:40,233
batch mode simply makes the batch bigger

240
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:43,533
so that it crafts less often to reduce lag

241
00:13:43,766 --> 00:13:46,500
like if the machine keeps crafting every tick

242
00:13:46,533 --> 00:13:50,666
it will make more lag rather than doing bigger batches less often

243
00:13:51,566 --> 00:13:53,466
and since this machine behaves like that

244
00:13:53,466 --> 00:13:56,200
you probably want to give it as much power as you can

245
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:59,733
and make sure you have one for personal usage

246
00:13:59,933 --> 00:14:04,700
so you can craft whatever you need without worrying too much or messing up any automation

247
